From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:23:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kodi: recover the Dolby Vision engine after a failure

One engine failure (a submission that returned -8, a frame that did not
complete within its wait, a failed reset) set m_unsafe: every later
picture was refused, the title stayed frozen until Kodi was restarted,
and the adapter could never be closed, so the engine and its leases
leaked. The engine's header allows more: after a failure every input
stays until dvvk_drain() succeeds and the engine is destroyed, and then
a new engine may be made.

Recover() does that. Close() on the engine drains (2 s) and destroys
it; only then are the frames in flight, the current picture and the
surface pools released, and the scanout slots told that an unfinished
write is over (dv_scanout_slots_drained, new: it counts as rejected
and no longer quarantines the buffers). The next picture starts a new
engine on the same scanout buffers, one of which may be on screen. Two
recoveries are allowed without a thousand good frames in between; a
third gives the title back to plain playback like a failed start.

The fail-stop remains where it has to: if the drain fails, work of the
engine may still read the decoded surfaces, so nothing is released and
no frame is taken. The drain is tried again when the display is handed
back (at most every ten seconds) and when the adapter is closed, so a
GPU that came back no longer leaks the engine.

A failed start, or a title given up as above, no longer turns Dolby
Vision off until Kodi restarts. The title restarts as plain playback
as before (now on every such failure, not only the first), the engine
stays off until that title has ended, and the next title tries again.
After three such titles in one Kodi run it stays off, with the
notification, as before; a missing library or another ABI still does
so at once.

When the engine reports that it could not attach its fence to a buffer
(dvvk_implicit_failed, an older kernel), the adapter returned without
waiting unless the GUI was read in place, so the commit could show an
unfinished buffer. It now waits for the ticket in that case too, as the
header asks.
